    "text": "This is a greedy, day-by-day simulation that only uses `impl` and `wait` tasks. It never moves services or creates binaries, which trades some potential score for guaranteed validity.\n\n**Feature order**\n- Each feature is split into one task per binary that holds its relevant services, using the initial binary assignment.\n- Features are sorted by `U \u00d7 (L \u2212 longest task) / total work`, where total work is the sum over its binaries of `D + R`.\n- Features whose single longest task cannot finish before `L` are dropped.\n\n**Daily simulation (days 0 \u2026 L\u22121)**\n1. Engineers whose task ends on day `t` are freed first. Their binary's active-engineer count is lowered before anyone new starts.\n2. Free engineers take tasks in ascending index order. This matches the statement's rule that the engineer listed earlier in the file starts first. It also lets the program compute `C` (engineers already working on that binary) for each new task.\n3. Each free engineer takes the next pending (feature, binary) task. When none are pending, the next feature in priority order is opened, but only if its estimated finish `t + max(D + R + C)` is before `L`.\n4. If a task of an opened feature can no longer finish before `L`, that whole feature is abandoned, so no more work is spent on it.\n5. Idle time before a task is written out as a single `wait`.\n\n**Validity**\n- Each (feature, binary) pair is assigned at most once, so no two engineers implement the same feature in the same binary.\n- No moves are made, so the move-related blocking rules never apply.\n- Every task lasts at least one day and starts before `L`, so each engineer has at most `L` tasks.\n- Engineers with no tasks are left out of the output.\n\n**Assumption:** an engineer whose task ends on day `t` does not count towards `C` on day `t`. If the grader counts them, some durations are off by one day. That costs a little score but cannot make the output invalid.\n\n```cpp\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Feat{\n    string name; int D; long long U;\n    vector<int> bins; long long work; int maxlen;\n};\nstruct Task{ int type; int f; int b; }; // type 0 = impl, 1 = wait (f = days)\n\nint main(){\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false); cin.tie(nullptr);\n    int L,G,S,B,F,N;\n    if(!(cin>>L>>G>>S>>B>>F>>N)) return 0;\n    unordered_map<string,int> sid; sid.reserve(S*2+10);\n    vector<int> sb(S);\n    vector<int> R(B,0);\n    for(int i=0;i<S;i++){string nm;int b;cin>>nm>>b;sid[nm]=i;sb[i]=b;R[b]++;}\n    vector<Feat> fs(F);\n    vector<int> mark(B,-1);\n    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){\n        int M; cin>>fs[i].name>>M>>fs[i].D>>fs[i].U;\n        for(int j=0;j<M;j++){\n            string nm;cin>>nm;\n            auto it=sid.find(nm);\n            if(it==sid.end()) continue;\n            int b=sb[it->second];\n            if(mark[b]!=i){mark[b]=i;fs[i].bins.push_back(b);}\n        }\n        auto &ft=fs[i];\n        sort(ft.bins.begin(),ft.bins.end(),[&](int a,int c){ if(R[a]!=R[c]) return R[a]>R[c]; return a<c;});\n        ft.work=0; ft.maxlen=0;\n        for(int b:ft.bins){ ft.work+=ft.D+R[b]; ft.maxlen=max(ft.maxlen,ft.D+R[b]); }\n    }\n    vector<int> order;\n    vector<double> key(F,0);\n    for(int i=0;i<F;i++){\n        if(fs[i].bins.empty()) continue;\n        if(fs[i].maxlen>=L) continue;\n        key[i]=(double)fs[i].U*(double)(L-fs[i].maxlen)/(double)fs[i].work;\n        order.push_back(i);\n    }\n    stable_sort(order.begin(),order.end(),[&](int a,int b){ if(key[a]!=key[b]) return key[a]>key[b]; return a<b;});\n\n    vector<int> cnt(B,0);\n    vector<vector<int>> bucket(L+1);\n    vector<int> curBin(G,-1), lastFree(G,0);\n    vector<vector<Task>> tasks(G);\n    vector<char> doomed(F,0);\n    deque<pair<int,int>> pending;\n    size_t ptr=0;\n    vector<int> idle(G); for(int i=0;i<G;i++) idle[i]=i;\n\n    for(int t=0;t<L;t++){\n        vector<int>& nw=bucket[t];\n        for(int e:nw){ cnt[curBin[e]]--; lastFree[e]=t; }\n        if(!nw.empty()){\n            sort(nw.begin(),nw.end());\n            vector<int> merged; merged.reserve(idle.size()+nw.size());\n            merge(idle.begin(),idle.end(),nw.begin(),nw.end(),back_inserter(merged));\n            idle.swap(merged);\n            vector<int>().swap(nw);\n        }\n        if(idle.empty()) continue;\n        if(pending.empty() && ptr>=order.size()) break;\n        vector<int> newIdle;\n        size_t k=0;\n        for(;k<idle.size();k++){\n            int e=idle[k];\n            int gf=-1,gb=-1,gd=0;\n            while(true){\n                while(!pending.empty()){\n                    auto pr=pending.front();\n                    if(doomed[pr.first]){pending.pop_front();continue;}\n                    int dur=fs[pr.first].D+R[pr.second]+cnt[pr.second];\n                    if(t+dur>=L){doomed[pr.first]=1;pending.pop_front();continue;}\n                    gf=pr.first;gb=pr.second;gd=dur;pending.pop_front();break;\n                }\n                if(gf>=0) break;\n                bool opened=false;\n                while(ptr<order.size()){\n                    int f=order[ptr++];\n                    int mx=0;\n                    for(int b:fs[f].bins) mx=max(mx,fs[f].D+R[b]+cnt[b]);\n                    if(t+mx<L){\n                        for(int b:fs[f].bins) pending.push_back({f,b});\n                        opened=true;break;\n                    }\n                }\n                if(!opened) break;\n            }\n            if(gf<0) break;\n            if(t>lastFree[e]) tasks[e].push_back({1,t-lastFree[e],0});\n            tasks[e].push_back({0,gf,gb});\n            cnt[gb]++;\n            curBin[e]=gb;\n            int end=t+gd;\n            if(end<L) bucket[end].push_back(e);\n        }\n        for(;k<idle.size();k++) newIdle.push_back(idle[k]);\n        idle.swap(newIdle);\n    }\n\n    string out;\n    int E=0;\n    for(int e=0;e<G;e++) if(!tasks[e].empty()) E++;\n    out+=to_string(E); out+='\\n';\n    for(int e=0;e<G;e++){\n        if(tasks[e].empty()) continue;\n        out+=to_string(tasks[e].size()); out+='\\n';\n        for(auto &tk:tasks[e]){\n            if(tk.type==1){ out+=\"wait \"; out+=to_string(tk.f); out+='\\n'; }\n            else { out+=\"impl \"; out+=fs[tk.f].name; out+=' '; out+=to_string(tk.b); out+='\\n'; }\n        }\n    }\n    fwrite(out.data(),1,out.size(),stdout);\n    return 0;\n}\n```",
